    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 the project has one test class (`AcceptanceTest`, 2 tests), and `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe locality derivation now prefers the postcode over the city.\n\n**`Localities.java`** \u2014 added a `locality(city, postcode)` method that:\n1. First looks up the region by postcode range via a new private `regionForPostcode` helper (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), returning that region when the postcode is a 4-digit value in a known range.\n2. Falls back to the existing `region(city)` city-to-region table when the postcode is absent, non-numeric, or in no known range (returning `UNKNOWN` for an unknown city).\n\n**`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 the `locality` mapping expression now calls `Localities.locality(owner.getCity(), owner.getPostcode())` instead of `Localities.region(owner.getCity())`.\n\nThis returns the same region for known cities (e.g. Sydney with postcode 2000 \u2192 NSW) while disambiguating same-named cities: an unknown city with a VIC-range postcode (3000) now resolves to VIC, as the two tests (`coreRegionFromPostcodeRange`, `functionalityPostcodePreferredOverCity`) verify. The existing `OwnerPostcode` validation logic is untouched, so postcode/city consistency checks still apply.",
