    "probe_text": "Here is the complete ordered pipeline for `POST /api/owners`, as wired in `owners.POST.yml` and implemented by the function classes. Every step runs under one shared `transaction` governance, so all writes commit once at the end (or roll back together on any thrown escalation).\n\n## 0. Endpoint guard (before any step)\n- **Authorization**: `hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')` (`composition.authorize`). Failure \u2192 `AuthorizationDeniedException` handler.\n\n## 1. `ValidateOwnerFields` \u2014 validation + normalization side-effects on the request body\nOrder within the step matters:\n1. **Normalize `address`** in place (`OwnerAddress.normalize`): trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`. (Done first so the blank check sees the normalized value, and the normalized form is what gets persisted/returned.)\n2. **Required-field check** \u2014 `firstName`, `lastName`, `address`, `city`, `telephone` must be non-null and non-blank; any missing \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (**400**, names the offending fields).\n3. **Normalize `telephone` to E.164** in place (`OwnerTelephone.toE164`): strip spaces/dashes/brackets; keep explicit `+` country code, else assume `+61` and drop one leading `0`; require 8\u201315 digits; for known country codes enforce national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210). Invalid \u2192 `InvalidOwnerTelephoneException` (**400**).\n4. **Normalize/validate `email`** in place if present (`OwnerEmail.normalize`): must match the address pattern, stored lower-cased; absent/blank allowed. Invalid \u2192 `InvalidOwnerEmailException` (**400**).\n5. **Validate `postcode`** if present (`OwnerPostcode.validate`): exactly 4 digits, and within the region range for known cities (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099); unknown city accepts any 4-digit; absent allowed. Invalid \u2192 `InvalidOwnerPostcodeException` (**400**).\n6. **Publishes** the mutated body (`Out<OwnerFieldsDto>`) for later steps.\n\n## 2. `EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity` \u2014 duplicate check\n- Resolves the household the request would join, builds `identityKey = canonicalTelephone|email|householdId`, and scans all owners. Exact whole-key match \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (**409**). (Consolidates the former separate telephone/email/household checks.)\n\n## 3. `EnsureCityCapacity` \u2014 capacity check\n- Counts existing owners in the request's `city`; if `\u2265 50` \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (**409**). (New owner not yet counted.)\n\n## 4. `EnsureDailyCreateLimit` \u2014 rate check\n- Effective registration date = supplied date else today, rolled forward to a business day (`BusinessDays.adjust`); counts owners already carrying that day; if `\u2265 100` \u2192 `DailyCreateLimitException` (**429**).\n\n## 5. `BuildOwner` \u2014 construct entity\n- Maps the DTO to an `Owner` (`OwnerMapper.toOwner`) and **sets `registrationDate`** to the business-day-adjusted effective date. Publishes `Out<Owner>`.\n\n## 6. `AssignOwnerCustomerCode` \u2014 mutate entity\n- Sets `customerCode` = `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, where `NNNN` = (owners already in that city) + 1, zero-padded to 4. (New owner not yet counted.)\n\n## 7. `AssignOwnerHousehold` \u2014 mutate entity + back-fill side-effect\n- Finds existing owners with the same normalized last name + address. If any:\n  - Sets this owner's `householdId` to the deterministic SHA-256-derived id.\n  - **Back-fills** that `householdId` onto any existing housemates lacking one, **saving each** (`ownerRepository.save(mate)`) \u2014 a write to other rows.\n  - Solo owner keeps `householdId = null`.\n\n## 8. `AssignOwnerNamesakeCount` \u2014 mutate entity\n- Sets `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners (excluding this one) with the same `firstName` + `lastName` (case-insensitive).\n\n## 9. `SaveOwner` \u2014 persist\n- `ownerRepository.save(owner)` \u2014 the primary insert (assigns the id).\n\n## 10. `AuditOwnerCreated` \u2014 logging side-effect\n- Emits an `AUDIT` logger info line with `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, and computed `membershipLevel` (`MembershipLevels.of`).\n\n## 11. `AssignOwnerBulkSignupWarning` \u2014 mutate entity (post-save)\n- Sets `bulkSignupWarning = true` if `> 80` owners share this registration date. Runs after save so the new owner is counted (matches what a later GET recomputes).\n\n## 12. `AssignOwnerHouseholdSize` \u2014 mutate entity (post-save)\n- Sets transient `householdSize` = count of owners sharing this `householdId` (including itself; solo = 1). Drives the GOLD tier (3+). Runs after save so the new owner is counted.\n\n## 13. `RespondWithOwnerCreated` \u2014 respond\n- Maps to `OwnerDto` and sends **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n---\n\n**Note on steps 11\u201312:** `bulkSignupWarning` and `householdSize` are set on the entity *after* `SaveOwner` but still under the same open transaction, so whether they are re-persisted depends on the JPA flush at commit rather than an explicit save call \u2014 worth keeping in mind if you were tracing exactly what lands in the database versus what's only reflected in the response body."
